<title>NETHERLANDS: Dutch capacity utilisation falls to 83.9 pct.</title>
<headline>Dutch capacity utilisation falls to 83.9 pct.</headline>
<dateline>VOORBURG, Netherlands 1997-01-31</dateline>
<text>
<p>Dutch manufacturing capacity utilisation fell to 83.9 percent in December from 84.5 percent in September, the Central Bureau of Statistics (CBS) said.  </p>
<p>DUTCH MANUFACTURING CAPACITY UTILISATION</p>
<p>					    Dec 96     Sep 96     Dec 95</p>
<p> Total manufacturing industry	83.9	 84.5	 83.7</p>
<p> - semi-manufactured goods	   82.8	 83.8	 81.4</p>
<p> - capital goods			 84.2	 85.8	 85.5</p>
<p> - consumer goods			84.9	 84.3	 85.3</p>
<p>Note - The CBS publishes capacity utilisation data once every three months.  </p>
<p>-- Amsterdam newsroom +31 20 504 5000, Fax +31 20 504 5040</p>
